  "term": "BEV",
  "definition": "BEV refers to a bird’s-eye-view representation used in perception systems, where sensor data such as LiDAR and camera information are organized from an overhead spatial perspective. In the source, BEV features are used to better align and combine information from different sensors for object detection.",
